  "verifiedContracts": [
    "Default and explicit receipt mode remain unchanged; a truncated receipt still fails structured settlement.",
    "Durable mode retains 50,000-character JSON independently of capped tool previews and supplies an isolated full value to host review; asynchronous schema transformation runs once.",
    "Guardrail and post-hook JSON rewrites become the candidate; stale ToolResult.data, raw inputs and injected result/provider metadata cannot mint retained evidence.",
    "Only a prepared direct call to the exact bound output-tool definition with the original structured_output name can mint the marker. Same-name replacements, unbound or legacy execution, renamed calls and nested execution cannot inherit it.",
    "Refusals, halts, post-hook errors, skips, invalid admission and cancellation observed before completion recording produce no marker. Sibling batches relay and inbound steering invalidates stale settlement.",
    "Full JSON is an opt-in live host event and persisted completion field, never a provider ToolMessage or StepToolResult field. Final output guardrails still clear accepted structured output.",
    "Strict records and collectors reject malformed JSON, unsafe numbers and contradictory success/name/skip/inputFailure/nested classifications. Later starts invalidate prior completion evidence.",
    "A real query cut at its actual completion recovers exact JSON and its bounded receipt without schema reexecution or duplicate completion. Resume still requests and reviews one fresh candidate.",
    "Legacy completion bytes and hashes are unchanged. A corrupt custom-log candidate produces an unknown outcome and does not authorize replay.",
    "Native durable configuration and unknown retention values fail before inference. An oversized post-hook candidate is refused by the session-record ceiling without acceptance."
  ],
  "initialCorrections": [
    "The oversized-result test first used a huge input, which hit the input-event limit. A small call with a huge post-hook JSON result now probes the intended completion-record limit.",
    "Early build and type checks encountered test fixtures still being authored: missing TokenUsage cached fields, pendingDecision shape, SessionRecord narrowing and a too-narrow ToolDefinition generic. Corrected fixtures and reran final workspace gates; no production workaround.",
    "The first documentation fence used a boolean review verdict without rejection feedback. Corrected it to the actual AnswerReview union and reran the fence gate."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The full JSON field is additional opt-in host-visible data; maxToolOutputChars does not cap that field.",
    "The 4 MiB session-record ceiling includes JSON escaping and metadata. Completion and inline settlement must fit; a write failure can reject query without a returned Turn or durable terminal record.",
    "Retention records execution evidence, not acceptance. An abort during asynchronous completion append may leave evidence, but later cancellation checks prevent acceptance.",
    "When marker is absent, durable settlement preserves the existing intact-receipt fallback, including host-provided output tools when the runtime tool is disabled. Exact-definition binding governs marker minting.",
    "Recovery preserves the marker but does not restore the original review dispatch snapshot or automatically settle a pre-crash candidate. Structured-result spilling and general typed ToolResult.data artifacts remain future work.",
    "This receipt does not claim activation of the open native Windows runtime, live model behavior or complete release CI validation. No push or publish was performed."
  ],
